// == TRACK 4 - LAYER 2 - MOTION ==============================================
// LIGHTCYCLE's engine-room hook. REWRITTEN from the broken-power-chord arp:
// that version ran root-5th-octave-5th in a bright square at c5-c6, and
// root-5th-octave in a clean square at that register is a music box — it read
// as CHRISTMAS, not as a grid at speed. Same notes, same rhythm, one octave
// down and one waveform over, and the genre flips.
//
// What replaced it is the trance workhorse: a ROLLING OCTAVE LINE. Sixteenth
// alternation between the root and the root an octave up, sawtooth, with the
// downbeat sixteenth of every beat DUCKED via a gain pattern. The duck is the
// point: it fakes the sidechain pump this genre is built on (superdough has no
// compressor), and the accent landing on the offbeat octave is what makes the
// line roll forward instead of march.
//
// Color tones only at bar EDGES: b7 and b2 as walk-ins to the next chord
// (a->g, a->bb, bb->a...). The body of every bar is pure root-octave — the
// hypnosis comes from repetition, and the mode is still stated by the bass and
// lead, not here.
//
// The multiplier trap does not apply here: each cell is a flat 16-element bar,
// one cell per cycle in the slowcat — nothing for `*n` to misplace.
setcps(0.5)
stack(
  // THE ROLLER. One flat cell per bar, 16 sixteenths each.
  note(`<[a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 g3 a4]
         [a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 g3 a4 bb3 a4]
         [bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 a3 bb4]
         [bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 bb3 bb4 c4 bb4 d4 bb4 c4 a3]
         [a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 g3 a4]
         [a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 a4 a3 g3]
         [g3 g4 g3 g4 g3 g4 g3 g4 g3 g4 g3 g4 g3 g4 f3 g4]
         [f3 f4 f3 f4 f3 f4 f3 f4 f3 f4 f3 f4 e3 f3 g3 a3]>`)
    .s("sawtooth")
    // The pump. Beat shape [duck accent mid accent]: the ear reads the hole on
    // the downbeat as compression breathing, same trick as the bass layer.
    .gain("[0.19 0.30 0.24 0.30]*4")
    .lpf(sine.range(700, 3400).slow(4)).lpq(9)
    .release(0.045)
    .delay(0.30).delaytime(0.375).delayfeedback(0.30)
    .pan(0.52).room(0.15).size(0.5),

  // THE STAB — filtered house chords on OFFBEAT EIGHTHS, the only voice on
  // that pulse. Fills the 200Hz-1kHz band nothing else occupies and separates
  // from the roller by rhythm (8ths vs 16ths) and by band (its filter tops out
  // where the roller's sweep starts reaching). Root-fifth-octave, no third:
  // the lead states the mode, the stab just pumps.
  note(`<[[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [bb3,f4,bb4]]*4]
         [[~ [bb3,f4,bb4]]*4]
         [[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [a3,e4,a4]]*4]
         [[~ [g3,d4,g4]]*4]
         [[~ [f3,c4,f4]]*4]>`)
    .s("sawtooth")
    .lpf(sine.range(520, 1150).slow(8)).lpq(11)
    .attack(0.002).decay(0.13).sustain(0)
    .gain(0.26).pan(0.44).room(0.2).size(0.55)
)
